(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the architecture of the Python programming language: CPython virtual machine, bytecode compilation \(.pyc\), and the interpreter execution cycle.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Python is an interpreted, high-level, object-oriented language with dynamic semantics. The) Tj
T*
(   standard reference implementation is CPython:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The Two-Stage Execution Pipeline:) Tj
T*
(   1. Compilation to Bytecode:) Tj
T*
(   - When a Python script \(`.py`\) is executed, the CPython compiler parses the human-readable) Tj
T*
(   source code into an Abstract Syntax Tree \(AST\).) Tj
T*
(   - The AST is then compiled into a platform-independent intermediate representation called) Tj
T*
(   Bytecode \(stored in `__pycache__/*.pyc` files\).) Tj
T*
(   - Bytecode consists of compact 1-byte or 2-byte opcodes \(such as LOAD_CONST, BINARY_ADD,) Tj
T*
(   STORE_NAME\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Python Virtual Machine \(PVM\):) Tj
T*
(   - The PVM is a software stack machine that reads the generated bytecode instructions) Tj
T*
(   sequentially.) Tj
T*
(   - The PVM interprets each bytecode instruction and executes the corresponding native machine) Tj
T*
(   code instructions on the host CPU.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Advantages for Electronics & Engineering:) Tj
T*
(   This architecture allows Python code written on a desktop workstation to run unmodified on) Tj
T*
(   embedded Linux single-board computers \(Raspberry Pi, BeagleBone, Jetson\) provided a compatible) Tj
T*
(   CPython interpreter is present.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Compare Interpreted vs Compiled languages, and analyze Python's dynamic typing vs C/C++'s static typing in embedded systems engineering.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Programming languages diverge significantly across translation models and type systems:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Compiled \(C/C++\) vs Interpreted \(Python\):) Tj
T*
(   - C/C++ compiles source code directly into native CPU binary machine code \(.exe / ELF\) via) Tj
T*
(   GCC/Clang. Execution is direct and lightning fast \(nanosecond level\), with minimal memory) Tj
T*
(   footprint, making it standard for hard real-time firmware and microcontrollers \(ARM Cortex-M,) Tj
T*
(   STM32, ESP32\).) Tj
T*
(   - Python compiles to intermediate bytecode interpreted by the PVM. Execution has interpreter) Tj
T*
(   overhead \(10x-50x slower in raw loops\), but offers rapid prototyping, interactive debugging,) Tj
T*
(   and extensive high-level libraries.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Static vs Dynamic Typing:) Tj
T*
(   - In C/C++, variables are statically declared \(`float adc_reading = 3.3f;`\). Types are fixed at) Tj
T*
(   compile time, guaranteeing zero runtime type errors and enabling extreme memory optimization in) Tj
T*
(   16KB RAM microcontrollers.) Tj
T*
(   - In Python, variables are dynamically typed \(`adc_reading = 3.3`\). The variable is merely a) Tj
T*
(   named reference pointing to a heap-allocated `PyObject`. The type is bound to the object value) Tj
T*
(   at runtime, facilitating rapid mathematical modeling and digital signal processing) Tj
T*
(   experimentation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
