(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail Python's scalar data types: int, float, complex, and bool, explaining their internal memory representations in CPython.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Python provides four primary primitive scalar numeric types, each represented as a) Tj
T*
(   heap-allocated C struct \(`PyObject`\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Integer \(int\):) Tj
T*
(   - Arbitrary Precision: Unlike C integers capped at 32/64 bits, Python integers have unlimited) Tj
T*
(   precision bounded only by available RAM.) Tj
T*
(   - Internal Struct: CPython implements `PyLongObject`, storing numbers as arrays of 30-bit) Tj
T*
(   digits. An integer `0` consumes 28 bytes in 64-bit systems due to metadata \(reference count,) Tj
T*
(   type pointer, size\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Floating-Point \(float\):) Tj
T*
(   - Implemented as a standard 64-bit double-precision IEEE 754 binary floating-point number) Tj
T*
(   \(`PyFloatObject`\), providing ~15 to 17 significant decimal digits of precision.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Complex Numbers \(complex\):) Tj
T*
(   - Formatted as `real + imag*1j`. Implemented as `PyComplexObject` encapsulating two 64-bit IEEE) Tj
T*
(   754 doubles \(`c.real` and `c.imag`\). Essential in ECE for AC circuit analysis, phasors, and) Tj
T*
(   Fourier transforms.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Boolean \(bool\):) Tj
T*
(   - Subclass of `int`. Has exactly two singleton instances: `True` \(integer value 1\) and `False`) Tj
T*
(   \(integer value 0\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Arithmetic, Relational, and Logical Operators in Python, detailing operator precedence and short-circuit evaluation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Operators perform computations on data operands:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Arithmetic Operators:) Tj
T*
(   - Addition \(`+`\), Subtraction \(`-`\), Multiplication \(`*`\), True Division \(`/`, returns float\),) Tj
T*
(   Floor Division \(`//`, truncates to integer\), Modulus \(`%`\), and Exponentiation \(`**`,) Tj
T*
(   right-to-left associativity\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Relational Operators:) Tj
T*
(   - Comparison operators \(`==`, `!=`, `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`\) evaluate to boolean `True` or) Tj
T*
(   `False`. Python supports chained comparisons: `0 <= voltage <= 5.0` is evaluated as `\(0 <=) Tj
T*
(   voltage\) and \(voltage <= 5.0\)`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Logical Operators & Short-Circuit Evaluation:) Tj
T*
(   - `and`: Returns the first falsy operand, or the last operand if all are truthy.) Tj
T*
(   - `or`: Returns the first truthy operand, or the last operand if all are falsy.) Tj
T*
(   - `not`: Inverts boolean state.) Tj
T*
(   - Short-circuiting guarantees that if the left operand of `and` is False, the right operand is) Tj
T*
(   NEVER evaluated, preventing NullPointer / IndexError exceptions: `if sensor is not None and) Tj
T*
(   sensor.read\(\) > 10:`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
ET

