(   2. Statements:) Tj
T*
(   - An executable action or instruction that alters program state:) Tj
T*
(   - Simple Statements: Contained within a single logical line \(e.g., `assignment`, `import sys`,) Tj
T*
(   `del x`, `pass`, `return`\).) Tj
T*
(   - Compound Statements: Span multiple lines with a header ending in a colon \(`:`\) followed by an) Tj
T*
(   indented block \(e.g., `if`, `for`, `def`, `class`\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. The LEGB Scope Resolution Hierarchy:) Tj
T*
(   When a variable identifier is resolved in Python, the interpreter searches four namespaces in) Tj
T*
(   strict sequence:) Tj
T*
(   - L \(Local\): Variables declared inside the current function.) Tj
T*
(   - E \(Enclosing\): Variables in outer enclosing nested functions \(closures\).) Tj
T*
(   - G \(Global\): Module-level variables defined at script top.) Tj
T*
(   - B \(Built-in\): Pre-loaded Python names \(`print`, `len`, `range`, `ValueError`\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
