(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Python's Decimal and Fraction modules, demonstrating how they eliminate precision loss in engineering calculations.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Standard floats cannot represent decimal fractions like 0.1 exactly. Python provides two exact) Tj
T*
(   arithmetic modules:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. The `decimal` Module \(Arbitrary Precision Decimal Arithmetic\):) Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   from decimal import Decimal, getcontext) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Set custom precision to 50 decimal digits) Tj
T*
(   getcontext\(\).prec = 50) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   v1 = Decimal\('0.1'\)) Tj
T*
(   v2 = Decimal\('0.2'\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(v1 + v2\) # Exactly 0.3 \(Zero rounding error!\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(v1 + v2 == Decimal\('0.3'\)\) # True!) Tj
T*
