(   [Problem Statement]: Detail Error and Exception Handling fundamentals in Python: try, except, else, finally, and custom exception classes.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Robust engineering software requires structured exception handling to gracefully manage) Tj
T*
(   hardware timeouts and communication failures:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Exception Handling Blocks:) Tj
T*
(   1. `try`: Encloses code that might trigger a runtime error.) Tj
T*
(   2. `except SpecificError as e`: Catches and handles specific exceptions without crashing the) Tj
T*
(   program.) Tj
T*
(   3. `else`: Executes strictly if the `try` block ran with ZERO exceptions.) Tj
T*
(   4. `finally`: Executes unconditionally, regardless of whether exceptions occurred or returns) Tj
T*
(   were executed \(ideal for releasing serial ports, files, and socket connections\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Engineering Example with Custom Exception:) Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   class SensorOvervoltageError\(Exception\):) Tj
T*
(   """Custom exception for hardware threshold violations.""") Tj
T*
(   pass) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def read_adc_channel\(voltage\):) Tj
T*
(   try:) Tj
T*
(   if voltage > 5.0:) Tj
T*
(   raise SensorOvervoltageError\(f'Voltage {voltage}V exceeds 5.0V maximum limit!'\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f'ADC sample accepted: {voltage} V'\)) Tj
T*
(   except SensorOvervoltageError as err:) Tj
T*
(   print\(f'SAFETY ALARM: {err}'\)) Tj
T*
(   finally:) Tj
T*
(   print\('Closing ADC hardware channel.'\)) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
