(   1. The Shebang Line \(`#!/usr/bin/env python3`\):) Tj
T*
(   Placed on the very first line of a Python script in Unix/Linux/Raspberry Pi OS. Instructs the) Tj
T*
(   operating system loader to locate the Python 3 binary in the user's environment and execute the) Tj
T*
(   script directly from the terminal without typing `python3 script.py`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The `if __name__ == '__main__':` Idiom:) Tj
T*
(   - When a script is executed directly from the terminal \(`python my_script.py`\), the CPython) Tj
T*
(   runtime assigns the special built-in string `'__main__'` to the module's `__name__` variable.) Tj
T*
(   - When the script is imported by another module \(`import my_script`\), `__name__` is set to the) Tj
T*
(   filename `'my_script'`.) Tj
T*
(   - By enclosing execution logic inside `if __name__ == '__main__':`, test code and main routines) Tj
T*
(   only run when executed directly, preventing accidental execution when imported by test suites.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
