(   [Problem Statement]: Demonstrate how to convert an analog ADC reading \(0?1023 on a 10-bit ADC\) to its corresponding physical Voltage \(0?5V\) using Python.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Scaling raw microcontroller ADC values to analog voltages:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   def adc_to_voltage\(raw_adc, resolution_bits=10, v_ref=5.0\):) Tj
T*
(   max_adc_val = \(1 << resolution_bits\) - 1 # 2^10 - 1 = 1023) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   if not \(0 <= raw_adc <= max_adc_val\):) Tj
T*
(   raise ValueError\(f'ADC value {raw_adc} out of range [0, {max_adc_val}]'\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   voltage = \(raw_adc / max_adc_val\) * v_ref) Tj
T*
(   return voltage) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Test sample values across 10-bit range) Tj
T*
(   samples = [0, 256, 512, 768, 1023]) Tj
T*
(   for s in samples:) Tj
T*
(   v = adc_to_voltage\(s, 10, 5.0\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f'ADC Code: {s:4d} -> Measured Voltage: {v:.3f} V'\)) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
